.TH PSLoadMNISTData 3 2023-12-01 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
PSLoadMNISTData

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/dataset.h>

.I
int  
.br
\fBPSLoadMNISTData\fR(\fIint type\fR, \fIconst char *images_file\fR, \fIconst char *labels_file\fR, \fIPSFloat ** data\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Load the MNIST dataset (\fIhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MNIST_database\fR) from files.
.br
The dataset files must be in gzip format (.gz): images data must be loaded from \fIimages_file\fR path and labels data must be loaded from \fIlabels_file\fR path.
.br
The dataset is allocated by the function itself and its pointer is stored into \fIdata\fR pointer-to-pointer (it cannot be \fINULL\fR). The length of the resulting dataset is returned by the function.
.br
The \fItype\fR argument can be used to tell if the dataset is a training dataset (\fIPS_DATA_TYPE_TRAINING\fR) or a test dataset (\fIPS_DATA_TYPE_TEST\fR).  

.SH RETURN VALUES
The length of the dataset (number of \fIPSFloat\fR elements) or zero if some error occurs.
Possibile errors:
.br

.RS 4
\[bu] The data argument is \fINULL\fR
.br

\[bu] Dataset files are \fINULL\fR, they don't exist or they cannot be opened.
.br

\[bu] Dataset cannot be allocated into memory
.br

\[bu] Dataset files are not in gzip format or some error occurs whil unzipping them.
.br

\[bu] The internal format of the dataset files format is not valid.
.br
.RE
